  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>PhSNa</mi></mover><mi>major</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>organic</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>compound</mi></math><p>Hence, it is confirmed that &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math>&#39; gives&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;reaction or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ArS</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;type reaction.</p><p><img height=\"96\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/95e50a50-f882-44b1-ae6b-c695bb184b33-image.png\" width=\"409\" /></p><p>The product of the bove reaction give positive Carius tube test.</p><p><img height=\"90\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/4d818004-4d35-45b8-b7ce-7e0996ef5788-image.png\" width=\"406\" /></p><p>The product of the bove reaction give positive Carius tube test.</p>",
